# WW360 accessible type scale

Audience includes utility/workforce reviewers who often need larger defaults. Prefer legibility over density.

## Scale (root 16px = 1rem)

| Role | Size | Notes |
|------|------|-------|
| Body / paragraphs | **1.125rem (18px)** | line-height **1.5–1.6** |
| UI (nav, buttons, labels, inputs) | **1rem–1.125rem** | Never below **1rem** on mobile form fields |
| Captions / kickers / metadata | **0.875rem (14px)** | Absolute floor for readable text |
| Headings | Larger than body | Keep clear hierarchy |

## Hard rules

- Never ship readable text below **0.875rem**
- Prefer `rem` (or `clamp()` with a **rem** term); avoid tiny `px` or `vw`-only sizes that fight browser zoom
- Touch targets ≥ **44×44px**
- Layouts must remain usable at **200% zoom** (WCAG 1.4.4)
- Do not shrink copy to fit aesthetics

## Tailwind mapping

- Body: `text-lg` (1.125rem) preferred; `text-base` (1rem) minimum
- UI controls: `text-base` minimum (avoid `text-sm` for primary actions)
- Captions only: `text-sm` (0.875rem); avoid `text-xs` for anything users must read

## Examples

```css
/* ❌ BAD — below floor */
.meta { font-size: 0.68rem; }
.btn { font-size: 0.85rem; }

/* ✅ GOOD */
.meta { font-size: 0.875rem; }
.btn { font-size: 1rem; }
.body { font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.55; }
```
